<h3>Research profile</h3>
<p>Researcher and educator working across <mark class="cv-highlight">human-centred design, experience design</mark>, software engineering and <mark class="cv-highlight">applied machine learning</mark>, with a background spanning engineering and design schools. Published research in HCI, visual-mathematical literacy, auxetic structures and transport modelling. Headed the M.Des Design Computation programme and set up the Experimental Maths Lab at Srishti Manipal Institute. Maintain Mathscapes as an independent mathematical practice.</p>



<h3>Research methods and technical skills</h3>
<p>Design and HCI: human-centred design, experience design, interaction design and physical computing.</p>
<p>Generative time-series modelling: Python, PyTorch and PyTorch Lightning for synthetic AQI data generation and transformer-based modelling.</p>
<p>Simulation-based machine learning: finite-element simulation data, K-means image labelling and logistic regression for deformation-mode detection.</p>
<p>Representation and feature design: visual representations, feature and label construction, and analysis of how representation choices shape model learning.</p>

